# Trivy ignore file — documented suppressions (ISO 27001 A.8.8 / T10)
#
# The convoyplan-updater image is built FROM docker:cli and bundles the
# docker-buildx and docker-compose CLI plugins. The vulnerabilities below live
# in those upstream-bundled plugin binaries (vendored containerd / moby / Go),
# not in our code, and cannot be patched by us without a fixed upstream
# docker:cli release. The updater container only runs our own trusted update
# scripts (git pull + `docker compose pull/up`); it does not parse untrusted
# MIME input, expose the moby authorization plugin API, or rely on
# runAsNonRoot — so none of these are exploitable here (VEX: not_affected).
#
# Re-evaluate once a patched docker:cli base image is available and drop the
# entries the bump resolves. Review by: 2026-09-10.

# containerd user ID handling bypass allows runAsNonRoot evasion.
# Bundled in docker-buildx/compose; the updater does not use runAsNonRoot.
# Fixed upstream in containerd 2.2.4.
CVE-2026-46680

# containerd OCI-spec violations allowing container escapes / privilege bypass
# (three related bugs). Bundled in docker-buildx and docker-compose plugins.
# The updater runs `docker compose pull/up` against trusted, operator-provided
# images only; it does not manage untrusted workloads that trigger these paths.
# Fixed upstream in containerd 2.2.5.
CVE-2026-53488
CVE-2026-53489
CVE-2026-53492

# Moby authorization bypass. Bundled docker engine libs; the updater image
# ships only the docker CLI — no dockerd / authz plugin endpoint is exposed.
# Fixed upstream in docker/moby 29.3.1.
CVE-2026-34040

# Go stdlib MIME header DoS (net/textproto). The updater parses no untrusted
# MIME input. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.11 / 1.26.4.
CVE-2026-42504

# Go stdlib x509 wildcard hostname verification bypass (VerifyHostname accepted
# wildcards for non-leaf certificates). Bundled in docker CLI Go binary. MITM
# requires network-level interposition between the updater and Docker Hub /
# GitHub; the updater runs inside the operator's trusted Docker network.
# Fixed upstream in Go 1.26.4.
CVE-2026-27145

# Go stdlib os.Root symlink-following / directory-traversal (os.Root followed
# symlinks it should have rejected). Bundled in the docker CLI Go binaries
# (docker / docker-buildx / docker-compose); the updater resolves no untrusted
# symlinked paths — it only runs `git pull` + `docker compose pull/up` on
# operator-trusted repositories and images. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.12 / 1.26.5.
CVE-2026-39822

# golang.org/x/crypto SSH server/client vulnerabilities (authenticated
# client loops, keyscan DoS, ssh/agent key restrictions bypass, etc.).
# Bundled in docker CLI Go binaries; the updater does not act as or connect
# to an SSH server or SSH agent — Git access goes over HTTPS.
# Fixed upstream in golang.org/x/crypto 0.52.0.
CVE-2026-39827
CVE-2026-39828
CVE-2026-39829
CVE-2026-39830
CVE-2026-39832
CVE-2026-39835
CVE-2026-42508
CVE-2026-46595
CVE-2026-46597

# golang.org/x/net HTML-parsing DoS / redirect bugs. Bundled in docker CLI
# Go binaries; the updater sends only structured API requests to Docker
# registry and GitHub — no untrusted HTML is parsed or rendered.
# Fixed upstream in golang.org/x/net 0.53.0–0.55.0.
CVE-2026-25680
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-42502
CVE-2026-42506

# gRPC-Go xDS RBAC and HTTP/2 vulnerabilities. Bundled in the docker-buildx and
# docker-compose plugin Go binaries; the updater only runs `docker compose
# pull/up` against operator-trusted images and never acts as an xDS-managed
# gRPC server or applies RBAC policies — the affected code paths are unreachable.
# Fixed upstream in google.golang.org/grpc 1.82.1.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf

# golang.org/x/text norm.Iter infinite loop on crafted input (DoS). Bundled in
# the docker-buildx/docker-compose plugin Go binaries; the updater only passes
# operator-trusted image refs and compose files to the docker CLI — it feeds no
# untrusted text through x/text normalization. Fixed upstream in
# golang.org/x/text 0.39.0.
CVE-2026-56852

# New batch picked up by a later docker:cli rebuild (2026-08): Go stdlib
# DoS/XSS issues and a moby/go-archive tar path-traversal bug, all bundled in
# the same docker/docker-buildx/docker-compose Go binaries as above. Same trust
# boundary: the updater only runs `git pull` + `docker compose pull/up` against
# operator-trusted repositories and images — it extracts no untrusted tar
# archives, parses no untrusted ASN.1/XML, renders no HTML templates, and
# reaches no untrusted URLs. The crypto/tls and dnsmessage DoS entries share
# the same network-interposition caveat as CVE-2026-27145 above. No fixed
# docker:cli tag exists yet. Review by: 2026-09-25.

# moby/go-archive: crafted tar archive can write outside the extraction
# directory. Bundled in docker-buildx; the updater extracts no untrusted tar
# archives. Fixed upstream in moby/go-archive 0.3.0.
CVE-2026-17106

# encoding/asn1: golang: Go encoding/asn1: Denial of Service via excessive
# recursion in Unmarshal. No untrusted ASN.1 input is parsed. Fixed upstream
# in Go 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-33818

# golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage: Denial of Service via invalid DNS record
# parsing. Requires a malicious DNS response; same network-interposition
# caveat as CVE-2026-27145. Fixed upstream in Go 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-46600

# net/http: Unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to Denial of Service.
# The updater only makes outbound HTTPS calls to Docker Hub / GitHub; it runs
# no HTTP server. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-56853

# html/template: Cross-Site Scripting via pathological input. The updater
# renders no HTML templates. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-56858

# encoding/xml: Denial of Service via XML decoding recursion depth issue. No
# untrusted XML is parsed. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-56859

# net/url: Denial of Service from quadratic complexity in path parsing. The
# updater parses only its own configured URLs, never untrusted input. Fixed
# upstream in Go 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-56860

# crypto/tls: Denial of Service via indefinite KeyUpdate messages. Requires a
# malicious/compromised TLS peer; same network-interposition caveat as
# CVE-2026-27145 above. Fixed upstream in Go 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0-rc3.
CVE-2026-56862

# golang.org/x/mod GOSUMDB/transparency-log verification bypass (a malicious
# GOSUMDB could serve arbitrary module content / bypass tile verification).
# Bundled in docker-buildx and docker-compose; the updater never runs `go
# build`/`go mod download` — it only executes the pre-built plugin binaries —
# so the GOSUMDB-verification code path is never exercised. Picked up by the
# same 2026-08 docker:cli rebuild as the batch above. Fixed upstream in
# golang.org/x/mod 0.40.0.
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# convoyplan-graphhopper: vulnerabilities bundled inside the upstream
# graphhopper-web JAR (graphhopper/Dockerfile, GH_VERSION pin). We cannot patch
# individual libraries inside the upstream fat JAR; fixing them requires a
# GraphHopper release that bumps these dependencies (evaluate a GH_VERSION
# upgrade — note that major bumps can change the graph format and force a
# re-import on every instance).
#
# Exposure assessment (VEX: not_affected): the GraphHopper container is only
# reachable inside the Docker network and on 127.0.0.1 (docker-compose.yml);
# the sole client is our backend sending well-formed routing requests. It never
# receives untrusted external traffic. The remaining input is the OSM PBF
# extract, downloaded over HTTPS from the operator-configured Geofabrik URL —
# worst case for the parser CVEs below is a DoS of the one-time graph import.
# Review by: 2026-09-10.

# jackson-core: StackoverflowError on deeply nested input. GraphHopper only
# parses its own config and our backend's requests. Fixed in jackson 2.15.0.
CVE-2025-52999

# protobuf-java: DoS in binary/textformat parsing. Used for OSM PBF import
# (trusted, operator-configured Geofabrik source); worst case import DoS.
CVE-2021-22569
CVE-2022-3509
CVE-2022-3510
CVE-2024-7254

# commons-io XmlStreamReader DoS on untrusted input — no untrusted XML reaches
# GraphHopper. Fixed in commons-io 2.14.0.
CVE-2024-47554

# Jetty HTTP request smuggling / gzip buffer corruption. Jetty serves only
# internal Docker-network requests from our backend — no untrusted clients,
# no intermediary proxy chain to smuggle through.
CVE-2026-2332
CVE-2024-13009

# Jetty Digest Authentication ISO-8859-1 lossy-encoding auth bypass. GraphHopper
# ships no Jetty security realm / Digest auth — it serves unauthenticated
# routing requests from our backend on the internal Docker network only, so the
# affected code path is never exercised. Fixed upstream in Jetty 9.4.63;
# requires a GraphHopper JAR release that bundles the patched Jetty.
CVE-2026-10050

# SnakeYAML Constructor deserialization RCE. GraphHopper parses only its own
# baked-in config.yml (trusted, ships in our image) — no untrusted YAML input.
CVE-2022-1471

# jackson-databind PolymorphicTypeValidator bypasses (generic type parameters
# and array subtype allowlist). GraphHopper uses Jackson to parse its own
# config and routing requests from our trusted backend only — no polymorphic
# deserialization of untrusted external data occurs. Fixed in jackson-databind
# 2.18.8; requires a GraphHopper JAR release that pulls the patched jackson.
CVE-2026-54512
CVE-2026-54513

# jackson-core async parser maxNumberLength bypass via chunked digit
# accumulation (incomplete fix for the earlier maxNumberLength DoS). Bundled in
# the upstream graphhopper.jar; GraphHopper only parses its own config and
# well-formed routing requests from our trusted backend on the internal Docker
# network — no untrusted JSON reaches the async parser. Fixed in jackson-core
# 2.18.8; requires a GraphHopper JAR release that pulls the patched jackson.
GHSA-r7wm-3cxj-wff9

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# convoyplan-frontend: vulnerability in the undici package bundled inside
# Node.js 26 (not an npm-installed dependency — Trivy reads Node's internal
# package.json for its built-in fetch implementation). Cannot be patched via
# npm overrides; requires a node:26-alpine image update that ships Node.js
# with undici >=6.27.0. The frontend container only calls our own backend API
# on the same Docker network — it does not fetch from attacker-controlled URLs.
# Re-evaluate once a patched node:26-alpine is available. Review by: 2026-09-10.

# undici Denial-of-Service via unbounded response memory allocation.
# Fixed upstream in undici 6.27.0 (bundled with a future Node.js 26.x release).
CVE-2026-12151

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# convoyplan-backend: msgpack is vendored *inside pip itself*
# (pip/_vendor/msgpack, see pip's vendor.txt) for pip's own internal wheel
# cache — it is not a project dependency and is never imported by the running
# FastAPI app. As of pip 26.2.1 (the latest release at time of review), pip
# still vendors msgpack==1.1.2; no pip release with a patched vendored
# msgpack exists yet, so there is nothing to bump on our side. The vendored
# copy is only exercised during `pip install` at image build time, not at
# container runtime — not exploitable here (VEX: not_affected).
# Re-evaluate once a pip release vendors a patched msgpack. Review by: 2026-09-10.

# msgpack: out-of-bounds read / crash on Unpacker reuse after an error.
# Fixed upstream in msgpack 1.2.1 (not yet adopted by pip's vendored copy).
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# convoyplan-backend: setuptools 70.3.0 (CVE-2025-47273 — path traversal in
# PackageIndex) keeps being reported even after backend/Dockerfile explicitly
# upgrades setuptools to >=78.1.1 before installing requirements — that
# upgrade replaces the copy actually importable in site-packages (verified:
# it shows up patched and clean in the scan), so the residual 70.3.0 finding
# comes from a second, bundled copy baked into the python:3.14-slim base
# image (CPython images carry their own setuptools wheel for ensurepip
# bootstrapping, separate from site-packages). That artifact is not
# importable by / part of this project's dependency graph, and is never
# executed at container runtime — the entrypoint only runs migrations +
# uvicorn, never pip/ensurepip, so PackageIndex's vulnerable code path is
# never reached (VEX: not_affected). Re-evaluate once a python:3.14-slim
# base image ships without the stale bundled copy. Review by: 2026-09-10.
CVE-2025-47273
